## Quick Start

### Installation

```bash
{% if is_diffusion %}
pip install mflux
{% else %}
pip install mlx-lm
{% endif %}
```

### Usage

{% if is_diffusion %}
```bash
# Generate image from text prompt
mflux-generate-qwen --model {{ hf_repo }} --prompt "A serene landscape at dusk with cinematic lighting"
```
{% else %}
#### CLI

```bash
# Chat interactively
mlx_lm.chat --model {{ hf_repo }}

# Generate text
mlx_lm.generate --model {{ hf_repo }} --prompt "Write a short poem about artificial intelligence."
```

#### Python API (with Chat Template)

```python
from mlx_lm import load, generate

model, tokenizer = load("{{ hf_repo }}")

messages = [
    {"role": "user", "content": "Explain quantum superposition in simple terms."}
]
prompt = tokenizer.apply_chat_template(
    messages, tokenize=False, add_generation_prompt=True
)

response = generate(model, tokenizer, prompt=prompt, verbose=True)
print(response)
```
{% endif %}

